    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of what I implemented for **version 2 of the owner identity**.\n\n## What changed\n\n**Version-2 region code (the mixing point)** \u2014 `Owner.java`\n- Added `IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` and `getIdentityRegion()`, which returns the plain region with the `V2` tag mixed in (e.g. `NSW \u2192 NSWV2`). Because `V2` is never a hex digit and the plain region never contains it, every identifier that embeds this code changes and can never reproduce a version-1 value.\n\n**The three identifiers now derive from the V2 region**\n- `memberId` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.memberIdFor`): region segment is now `getIdentityRegion()` \u2192 `NSW2616E6609E3` became `NSWV22616E6609E9` (Luhn check digit recomputed too).\n- `identityKey` (`Owner.getIdentityKey`): SHA-256 input now prefixed with `identityRegion|\u2026`.\n- `householdId` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.householdIdFor`): SHA-256 input now prefixed with the identity region.\n\n**User-facing region fields stay plain (no V2 tag)** \u2014 `Owner.java`\n- `getLocality()` no longer reads the region back off the memberId (which now carries `V2`); it returns the plain `getRegion()` (`NSW`). `timezone` and `ownerSegment`'s area derive from that, so they stay correct \u2014 this is the owner-segment recompute the spec called for.\n\n**Response shape** \u2014 `openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper.java`\n- Added a new `OwnerIdentity` schema; moved `memberId`, `identityKey`, `householdId` off the top level into a nested `identity` object.\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion` = 2. The mapper populates both via `toOwnerIdentity(...)` and an `apiVersion` expression.\n\n**Audit schema v2** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.ownerCreatedEvent`\n- The structured `OWNER_CREATED` event now includes `\"schemaVersion\":2` and `\"ownerSegment\"` recomputed from the version-2 identity.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. The provided `AcceptanceTest` (apiVersion=2, identity grouping, no top-level identifiers) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
